Mental model
NixOS compiles systemd units directly from Nix attribute sets into /nix/store: 1. Unit Definition: Declared under systemd.services.&lt;name&gt;. 2. Auto-Reloading: When nixos-rebuild switch runs, NixOS compares the old systemd unit with the new one in /nix/store. If the unit changed, it restarts or reloads the service automatically. 3. Hardened Sandboxing: Systemd security flags (ProtectSystem, ProtectHome, NoNewPrivileges, PrivateTmp) are first-class attributes.
systemd.services.desk-api = {
  wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];
  after = [ "network.target" ];
