Mental model
In traditional Linux: - /etc/passwd and /etc/shadow are mutated by useradd and passwd. - If an employee leaves the company, an administrator must remember to log into every server and delete their account.
In NixOS: 1. Declarative Accounts: Users are declared in users.users.&lt;name&gt;. 2. Immutable Passwords & Users (users.mutableUsers = false;): When set to false, /etc/passwd is rewritten completely from your Nix configuration on every nixos-rebuild. Any user account removed from Git is purged from the machine instantly. 3. Authorized Keys: Public keys are declared directly in code (openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = [ "ssh-ed25519 ..." ];).
users.users.alice = {
  isNormalUser = true;
  extraGroups = [ "wheel" ];
  openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = [ "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5..." ];
};

